=begin
  fizzlocksmehr.lic -- Locksmehr Larceny quest (Wehnimer's Landing, weekly, level 20+)

  Fork of Drafix's locksmehrquest.lic 1.0.4. Changes:
    * Resumes from wherever the quest is (reads QUEST INFO), so a killed or
      crashed run picks up on the trail or at the turn-in, not back at the dock.
      Accepts the quest itself if it is Available.
    * Fights with a stripped-down bigshot setup: for the run, the hunting prep
      commands are blanked (bigshot quick runs them before every fight, which
      meant Fizzleworth-prep after each search) and restored on exit, even when
      killed. Uses your Quick Hunting Commands, or a plain fallback if blank.
    * One SEARCH per attempt. The original re-sent SEARCH on every "...wait"
      line, which flooded the game with dozens of searches per room.
    * Walks the trail itself (no step2 needed) and compares room ids as numbers,
      so it stops at the end of the trail instead of hanging there.
    * Puts the crate in your stow container, or your disk if STOW fails, and
      gets it back out at the Merchant's Guild before RAISE.

  0.2 (2026-11-27), after the first live run killed Fizzleworth at the ambush
  (five highwaymen and marauders; bigshot opened with a Voln symbol, he never
  cast, and was dead 10 s later):
    * Opens every fight with 2+ standing foes with Grasp of the Grave (709)
      the moment the ambush or boss shows, before bigshot starts. That is what
      Scott typed by hand (`quak`) in the July and 11-20 ambushes.
    * Voln symbols (bigshot's Signs) are cast before each search instead, and
      blanked in bigshot for the run.
    * Before each search: health 95%+, no bleeding, no wound worse than minor
      (eherbs --buy=off, twice at most), mana for 709 plus follow-ups, no
      roundtime, not stunned. Waits up to 10 min, then stops; run it again to
      carry on.
    * Stops the moment you are dead (it used to keep running bigshot, search
      and walk while dead).

  0.3 (2026-11-27):
    * Runs Fizzleworth-prep with the scroll spell-up (`quest scrolls`) before
      the dock, cabin or trail; not when only the turn-in is left.
    * Reanimates the last bandit standing in a fight (;reanim: Pain, Animate
      Dead, the minor demon hands it UserVars.reanim_weapon, the claidhmore),
      once a run, never the boss; `;reanim die` puts the claidhmore back on
      the demon once the crate is found, before town.
    * A death or a stop leaves the quest In Progress (no cooldown until it is
      completed), so just run it again.

  Usage:
    ;fizzlocksmehr            run or resume the quest
    ;fizzlocksmehr complete   also send QUEST COMPLETE at the end

  Game text verified from Fizzleworth's 2026-07-10 run and the 2026-11-20
  locksmehrquest run: dock and cabin QUEST CONTINUE text, trail search results,
  the bandit ambush and the boss, "You've found the missing cargo!", and the
  RAISE turn-in in the Merchant's Guild foyer. 0.2: Grasp of the Grave success
  text and the cast refusals ("...wait N seconds.", "Wait N sec.", "You are
  still stunned.", "can't think clearly enough", entangled in a web), and the
  Symbol of Courage/Protection replies, all from Fizzleworth's saga logs.

     author: Fizzleworth (fork of Drafix's locksmehrquest)
       game: Gemstone
       tags: quests
    version: 0.3
=end

module FizzLocksmehr
  # Lich keeps the module between runs; only define the constants once.
  unless const_defined?(:QUEST, false)
  QUEST       = 'Locksmehr Larceny'
  DOCK        = 36718 # Boatyard Dock (u556001)
  CABIN       = 9620  # A Rustic Cabin, Davlan (u13000003)
  TRAIL_START = 1185  # Locksmehr River Trail, just before the first clue room (1183)
  TRAIL_END   = 1157  # far end of the trail; crate was at 1167 on 07-10
  TRAIL_ROOMS = (1157..1188).to_a
  GUILD       = 8626  # Merchant's Guild, Foyer (u4034)

  FALLBACK_QUICK = '710 target, 701 target, 702 target'

  STAGE_TEXT = {
    dock:   /Seek out the merchant's assistant at the Boatyard Dock/,
    cabin:  /Seek out Davlan/,
    turnin: /You've found the missing cargo/,
    trail:  /search for any trace of the stolen cargo|tracked down the bandits|SEARCH for the stolen cargo|bandit boss/i
  }

  SEARCH_RESULTS = [
    [:crate,   /You've found the missing cargo!|A sturdy mithril-banded crate is now in your/],
    [:ambush,  /find a group of bandits lying in wait!/],
    [:boss,    /^You search the area for a moment\.\.\.\s*$/],
    [:already, /You have already searched this room\./],
    [:nothing, /You don't find anything of interest|You do not find anything of interest/],
    [:clue,    /deep rut (?:in|along) the trail|You quickly scour the area|You search the area|You find some deep footprints|You spend some time searching/]
  ]
  end

  def self.msg(text)
    respond "[fizzlocksmehr] #{text}"
  end

  def self.elapsed
    m, s = (Time.now - @started).to_i.divmod(60)
    format('%d:%02d', m, s)
  end

  # ---- bigshot: stripped-down setup for the run -------------------------

  def self.swap_bigshot_settings
    UserVars.op ||= {}
    # A previous run that died without restoring leaves its saved copy behind.
    if UserVars.fizzlocksmehr_saved.is_a?(Hash)
      UserVars.fizzlocksmehr_saved.each { |k, v| UserVars.op[k] = v }
      msg 'Restored bigshot settings left over from an earlier run.'
    end
    saved = {
      'hunting_prep_commands' => UserVars.op['hunting_prep_commands'],
      'quick_commands'        => UserVars.op['quick_commands'],
      'quickhunt_targets'     => UserVars.op['quickhunt_targets'],
      'signs'                 => UserVars.op['signs']
    }
    UserVars.fizzlocksmehr_saved = saved
    @signs = saved['signs'].to_s
    UserVars.op['hunting_prep_commands'] = ''
    UserVars.op['quickhunt_targets'] = ''
    # bigshot casts its Signs first in every fight; 11-27 that was the opening
    # it needed for a Grasp. They go up before each search instead.
    UserVars.op['signs'] = ''
    UserVars.op['quick_commands'] = FALLBACK_QUICK if UserVars.op['quick_commands'].to_s.strip.empty?
    msg "Bigshot for this run: no hunting prep, no Signs (#{@signs.empty? ? 'none set' : "#{@signs} cast before each search"}), " \
        "quick commands: #{UserVars.op['quick_commands']}"
  end

  def self.restore_bigshot_settings
    saved = UserVars.fizzlocksmehr_saved
    return unless saved.is_a?(Hash)

    UserVars.op ||= {}
    saved.each { |k, v| UserVars.op[k] = v }
    UserVars.fizzlocksmehr_saved = nil
  end

  # Same filter as fizzreim: never count your own animate or minor demon
  # (a verlok, or one wearing the raven illusion).
  def self.hostiles
    GameObj.targets.to_a.select { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name.to_s !~ /animated|verlok|minor demon|raven/i }
  end

  def self.foes?
    hostiles.any?
  end

  def self.dead_stop!
    return unless checkdead

    msg 'You are dead: stopping.'
    exit
  end

  def self.wait_for_foes(seconds)
    deadline = Time.now + seconds
    sleep 0.1 until foes? || Time.now > deadline
    foes?
  end

  # ---- Grasp of the Grave (709) -------------------------------------------

  def self.grasp_known?
    Spell[709].known?
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def self.grasp_cost
    cost = Spell[709].mana_cost.to_i
    cost.positive? ? cost : 9
  rescue StandardError
    9
  end

  def self.standing_foes
    hostiles.reject { |t| t.status.to_s =~ /lying|prone|sitting|kneeling/i }
  end

  # The cast's own end line, or a refusal (all seen in Fizzleworth's logs).
  def self.cast_done?(line)
    line =~ /Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Roundtime: \d+ sec|^\.\.\.wait \d+ sec|^Wait \d+ sec|You are still stunned|can't think clearly enough to prepare|You can't do that while entangled|don't have a spell prepared|You can't cast|You have no/i
  end

  def self.cast_collect(cmd, timeout = 6)
    lines = []
    clear
    put cmd
    deadline = Time.now + timeout
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      unless line
        sleep 0.05
        next
      end
      lines << line
      break if cast_done?(line)
    end
    lines.join("\n")
  end

  # Drags the whole room down. Cast when 2+ foes are standing, at most every
  # 6 s. Returns true if it went off.
  def self.grasp_if_crowd
    return false unless grasp_known?
    return false if standing_foes.size < 2
    return false if @last_grasp && Time.now - @last_grasp < 6

    4.times do
      dead_stop!
      if Char.mana.to_i < grasp_cost
        msg "Only #{Char.mana} mana: no Grasp of the Grave."
        return false
      end
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      sleep 0.2 while checkstunned && !checkdead
      dead_stop!
      fput 'release' if checkprep != 'None'
      text = cast_collect('incant 709')
      if text =~ /arms grab at whatever they can/
        @last_grasp = Time.now
        msg "Grasp of the Grave: #{text.scan(/The arms snatch viciously at .+? and drag/).size} dragged down."
        return true
      elsif text =~ /^(?:\.\.\.wait|Wait) (\d+) sec/i
        sleep Regexp.last_match(1).to_i + 0.2
      elsif text =~ /You are still stunned|You can't do that while entangled/
        sleep 0.5
      elsif text =~ /can't think clearly enough to prepare/
        Script.run('eherbs', '--spellcast --buy=off')
      else
        @last_grasp = Time.now
        msg "Grasp of the Grave did not go off: #{text.lines.last.to_s.strip}"
        return false
      end
    end
    false
  end

  # ---- reanimate one bandit ----------------------------------------------
  # ;reanim kills it with Pain (711), raises it with Animate Dead (730) and has
  # the minor demon drop the spare weapon for it (UserVars.reanim_weapon:
  # claidhmore for Fizzleworth). It blocks ~20 s, so only on the LAST bandit
  # standing (Fizzleworth-attack-ultima's rule), never the boss, once a run.

  def self.animate_here?
    GameObj.npcs.to_a.any? { |n| n && n.name.to_s =~ /\banimate/i }
  end

  def self.reanim_wanted?
    return false if @reanim_tried
    return false if animate_here?

    Script.exists?('reanim') && Spell[711].known? && Spell[730].known?
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def self.reanim_target
    left = hostiles
    return nil unless left.size == 1
    # gameobj-data types the ambush bandits "aggressive npc,bandit"; not a
    # wandering boar, and not the boss
    return nil unless left.first.type.to_s =~ /bandit/
    return nil if left.first.name.to_s =~ /bandit boss/i

    left.first
  end

  def self.reanimate(foe)
    @reanim_tried = true
    msg "Reanimating the #{foe.name.to_s.sub(/\A(?:an?|the) /i, '')} (weapon: #{UserVars.reanim_weapon})."
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    Script.run('reanim', "##{foe.id}")
    dead_stop!
    msg(animate_here? ? 'Animate is up.' : 'No animate raised.')
  end

  def self.dismiss_animate
    return unless $reanim_animate_live && Script.exists?('reanim')

    msg 'Dismissing the animate (claidhmore back to the demon) before town.'
    Script.run('reanim', 'die')
  end

  # One bigshot quick. While a reanimate is still wanted, stop it as soon as
  # only one bandit is left standing in the room, so ;reanim can have it.
  def self.bigshot_quick
    Script.start('bigshot', 'quick')
    deadline = Time.now + 3
    sleep 0.05 until Script.running?('bigshot') || Time.now > deadline
    while Script.running?('bigshot')
      if checkdead || (reanim_wanted? && reanim_target)
        Script.kill('bigshot')
        deadline = Time.now + 5
        sleep 0.1 while Script.running?('bigshot') && Time.now < deadline
        break
      end
      sleep 0.2
    end
  end

  # Grasp first whenever 2+ are standing, then bigshot quick until nothing
  # hostile is left (reanimating the last bandit once a run). Bandits hide, so
  # look again after a short pause before calling it clear.
  def self.fight
    runs = 0
    loop do
      dead_stop!
      unless foes?
        sleep 2
        dead_stop!
        break unless foes?
      end
      grasp_if_crowd
      dead_stop!
      if reanim_wanted? && (foe = reanim_target)
        reanimate(foe)
        next
      end
      runs += 1
      if runs > 8
        msg 'Still hostiles after 8 bigshot runs; carrying on.'
        break
      end
      waitrt?
      bigshot_quick
      sleep 0.5
    end
  end

  # ---- before each search -------------------------------------------------

  def self.min_mana
    grasp_cost + 50
  end

  def self.wounded?
    XMLData.injuries.to_h.any? { |_, v| v.is_a?(Hash) && v['wound'].to_i > 1 }
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  def self.hurt?
    Char.percent_health.to_i < 95 || checkbleeding || wounded?
  end

  def self.status_line
    "health #{Char.percent_health}%#{', bleeding' if checkbleeding}#{', wounded' if wounded?}, mana #{Char.mana} (need #{min_mana})"
  end

  # bigshot's Signs (Voln symbols for Fizzleworth), plain spell numbers only.
  def self.cast_symbols
    @signs.to_s.split(',').map(&:strip).grep(/\A\d+\z/).each do |num|
      sign = Spell[num.to_i]
      next unless sign && sign.known? && !sign.active? && sign.affordable?

      dead_stop!
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      sign.cast
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    msg "Signs: #{e.message}"
  end

  def self.ready_to_search
    herbed = 0
    fights = 0
    deadline = Time.now + 600
    noted = Time.at(0)
    loop do
      dead_stop!
      if foes? && fights < 2
        fights += 1
        fight
        next
      end
      break if !hurt? && Char.mana.to_i >= min_mana

      if hurt? && herbed < 2 && Script.exists?('eherbs')
        herbed += 1
        msg "Healing before the next search (#{status_line})."
        Script.run('eherbs', '--buy=off')
        next
      end
      if Time.now > deadline
        msg "Not ready to search after 10 min (#{status_line}). Stopping; run ;fizzlocksmehr again to carry on from here."
        exit
      end
      if Time.now - noted > 60
        msg "Waiting before the next search: #{status_line}."
        noted = Time.now
      end
      sleep 2
    end
    cast_symbols
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    sleep 0.2 while checkstunned && !checkdead
    dead_stop!
  end

  # ---- quest state ------------------------------------------------------

  def self.strip(lines)
    Array(lines).map { |l| l.to_s.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').gsub('&gt;', '>').gsub('&lt;', '<') }
  end

  def self.quest_number_and_status
    lines = strip(Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml('quest list', /Quest Name|You have no quests|no available quests/i, /QUEST ABANDON|<prompt/))
    row = lines.find { |l| l =~ /#{QUEST}/ }
    return [nil, nil] unless row && row =~ /(\d+)\)\s+#{QUEST}\s+(Available|In Progress|Complete|Cooldown)/i

    [Regexp.last_match(1).to_i, Regexp.last_match(2)]
  end

  def self.quest_stage
    num, status = quest_number_and_status
    return :missing if num.nil?
    return :complete if status =~ /Complete/i
    return :accept if status =~ /Available/i

    info = strip(Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("quest info #{num}", /Name:/, /<prompt/)).join("\n")
    return :complete if info =~ /You have completed this quest/
    STAGE_TEXT.each { |stage, re| return stage if info =~ re }
    msg "Unrecognised quest step; treating it as the trail search:\n#{info.lines.last(2).join}"
    :trail
  end

  def self.quest_continue(times)
    times.times do
      dead_stop!
      waitrt?
      fput 'quest continue'
      sleep 0.5
    end
    waitrt?
  end

  # ---- trail ------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.read_until(patterns, timeout)
    deadline = Time.now + timeout
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      unless line
        sleep 0.05
        next
      end
      patterns.each { |key, re| return [key, line] if line =~ re }
    end
    [:timeout, nil]
  end

  # One SEARCH; on "...wait N" it sleeps the N seconds and sends one more.
  def self.search
    3.times do
      waitrt?
      clear
      put 'search'
      key, line = read_until(SEARCH_RESULTS + [[:wait, /^\.\.\.wait (\d+) sec/]], 8)
      if key == :wait
        sleep(line[/\d+/].to_i + 0.3)
        next
      end
      waitrt?
      return key
    end
    :timeout
  end

  # Takes one step toward dest. Returns true if it moved.
  def self.step_toward(dest)
    dead_stop!
    here = Room.current
    path = here&.path_to(dest)
    return false if path.nil? || path.empty?

    way = here.wayto[path.first.to_s]
    before = XMLData.room_count
    waitrt?
    if way.is_a?(StringProc)
      way.call
    else
      move way
    end
    deadline = Time.now + 5
    sleep 0.1 until XMLData.room_count > before || Time.now > deadline
    XMLData.room_count > before
  end

  def self.room_searchable?(lines)
    lines.any? { |l| l =~ /The area looks well suited to a search\./ }
  end

  # The "well suited" line comes with the room text; HELP of a missing topic
  # gives a fixed reply that marks the end of it.
  def self.arrival_lines
    put 'help lag-check'
    lines = []
    deadline = Time.now + 5
    while Time.now < deadline
      line = get?
      unless line
        sleep 0.05
        next
      end
      lines << line
      break if line =~ /No help files matching/
    end
    lines
  end

  def self.handle_crate
    waitrt?
    return unless [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].any? { |h| h.name.to_s =~ /crate/ }

    fput 'stow crate'
    sleep 0.5
    return unless [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].any? { |h| h.name.to_s =~ /crate/ }

    if GameObj.loot.to_a.any? { |o| o.noun == 'disk' && o.name =~ /#{Char.name}/i }
      fput 'put crate in disk'
    else
      msg 'Could not stow the crate; carrying it in hand.'
    end
  end

  # Ready check, SEARCH, and if that springs an ambush or the boss, fight at
  # once (Grasp first) and search the room again. Three searches at most.
  def self.search_here
    3.times do |n|
      ready_to_search
      result = search
      dead_stop!
      msg "#{Room.current.id}: search#{' again' if n.positive?} -> #{result} (#{elapsed})"
      return :crate if result == :crate

      if %i[ambush boss].include?(result)
        wait_for_foes(2)
      else
        sleep 1
      end
      return result unless foes?

      fight
    end
    :gave_up
  end

  def self.do_trail
    Script.run('go2', TRAIL_START.to_s) unless TRAIL_ROOMS.include?(Room.current.id.to_i)
    fight if foes?
    clear
    # Search the room we start in (a resumed run may stop mid-trail).
    return true if search_here == :crate

    until Room.current.id.to_i == TRAIL_END
      dead_stop!
      clear
      unless step_toward(TRAIL_END)
        msg "Could not step toward #{TRAIL_END} from #{Room.current.id}."
        return false
      end
      next unless room_searchable?(arrival_lines)

      return true if search_here == :crate
    end
    msg "Reached the end of the trail (#{TRAIL_END}) without the crate."
    false
  end

  # ---- turn-in ----------------------------------------------------------

  def self.crate_in_hand?
    [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].any? { |h| h.name.to_s =~ /crate/ }
  end

  def self.do_turnin
    Script.run('go2', GUILD.to_s)
    unless Room.current.id.to_i == GUILD
      msg "Not in the Merchant's Guild foyer (#{GUILD}); stopping."
      return false
    end
    unless crate_in_hand?
      empty_hands
      fput 'get my crate'
      fput 'get crate from disk' unless crate_in_hand?
    end
    unless crate_in_hand?
      msg 'Could not find the crate to RAISE.'
      return false
    end
    waitrt?
    result = dothistimeout('raise crate', 10, /Locksmehr Larceny is finished|You raise your/)
    waitrt?
    fill_hands
    if result =~ /finished/
      msg "Quest finished in #{elapsed}."
      true
    else
      msg "RAISE did not finish the quest: #{result.inspect}"
      false
    end
  end

  # ---- main -------------------------------------------------------------

  # Full prep with the scroll spell-up forced on (`scrolls`), before any
  # fighting: spells, rubs, lifeguard, the demon told to follow (;reanim needs
  # it there to hand over the claidhmore) and Fizzleworth-buyweapon if the
  # demon has no spare. Any mode word but here/arena/sever is the full prep.
  def self.prep
    name = "#{Char.name}-prep"
    unless Script.exists?(name)
      msg "No #{name} script; skipping the prep."
      return
    end
    msg "#{name} with the scroll spell-up first."
    Script.run(name, 'quest scrolls')
    dead_stop!
  end

  def self.run(vars)
    @started = Time.now
    @last_grasp = nil
    @reanim_tried = false
    dead_stop!
    swap_bigshot_settings
    stage = quest_stage
    msg "Quest step: #{stage}"
    case stage
    when :missing
      msg "#{QUEST} is not in QUEST LIST (under level 20, or already completed this week)."
      return
    when :complete
      msg 'Already complete: use QUEST COMPLETE to claim rewards.' unless vars.include?('complete')
    end

    prep if %i[accept dock cabin trail].include?(stage)

    if stage == :accept
      num, = quest_number_and_status
      fput "quest accept #{num}"
      stage = :dock
    end

    if stage == :dock
      Script.run('go2', DOCK.to_s)
      quest_continue(2)
      stage = :cabin
    end

    if stage == :cabin
      Script.run('go2', CABIN.to_s)
      quest_continue(2)
      stage = :trail
    end

    if stage == :trail
      return unless do_trail

      handle_crate
      dismiss_animate
      stage = :turnin
    end

    if stage == :turnin
      return unless do_turnin

      stage = :complete
    end

    if stage == :complete && vars.include?('complete')
      waitrt?
      fput 'quest complete'
    elsif stage == :complete
      msg 'Use QUEST COMPLETE to claim the rewards.'
    end
  end
end

before_dying { FizzLocksmehr.restore_bigshot_settings }

FizzLocksmehr.run(Script.current.vars[1..].to_a.map(&:downcase))
